# Menu titles use Title Case (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-05): **all menu titles** must use
**Title Case** — capitalize the first letter of each word. Admin SPA
menus were inconsistent (sentence case mixed with Title Case among
siblings).

## The rule

> **Every navigation menu item, sidebar label, and top-level menu title
> in operator GUIs — especially `pim-offline-server/ui` — uses US English
> Title Case: capitalize the first letter of each word. Default is
> capitalize every word (as Phil stated). Keep short conjunctions or
> prepositions lowercase only when an existing design-system token
> already does so for that exact string; otherwise capitalize each
> word.**

Applies to:

| Surface | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| Admin SPA sidebar | `ui/src/config/menuItems.tsx` and any shared nav that feeds the drawer |
| Section hub / quick-access labels | When they reuse or mirror the same menu title strings |
| Win32 / Tauri configurator menus | Menu bar and tree labels that act as navigation |
| Future operator GUIs | Same Title Case bar for new nav config |

Does **not** require rewriting page H1 / body copy unless that string is
the **same source** as the menu label (shared constant or identical
config field). Form field labels, chip statuses, and dialog titles are
out of scope unless they are navigation menu titles.

## Required pattern

```tsx
// Good — Title Case
{ path: '/pam/connection-points', label: 'Connection Points' }
{ label: 'Proxied Access', children: [/* … */] }
{ path: '/settings/platform', label: 'Server Configuration' }

// Bad — sentence case
{ path: '/pam/connection-points', label: 'Connection points' }
{ label: 'Proxied access', children: [/* … */] }

// Bad — ALL CAPS
{ label: 'PROXIED ACCESS', children: [/* … */] }
```

Acronyms already in product vocabulary stay as acronyms inside Title
Case (`IAM`, `SSH`, `RDP`, `OCR`, `HSM`, `VM`, `IR`). Em dashes and
ampersands do not change the Title Case duty on the surrounding words
(`Recording Agents — Health`, `Jump Fleet & Load Balancing`).

## Forbidden constructs

In nav / sidebar / top-level menu config (new menus and edits to
existing nav):

- **ALL CAPS** menu titles
- **Sentence case** for multi-word menu items (`Report templates`,
  `Proxied access`, `Server configuration`)
- **Inconsistent casing** across sibling items in the same menu level
  (one Title Case, one sentence case)

## Required agent behavior

1. When adding or editing a nav item, write the `label` (or equivalent
   i18n string used as the menu title) in Title Case in the same change
   set.
2. Prefer one canonical nav config (`menuItems.tsx` or shared kit) so
   section landings / quick access that mirror menu titles stay in sync.
3. Do not “fix casing later” — nav Title Case lands with the menu
   change.
4. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` when editing the
   workspace copy ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

